Date: Sun, 3 Aug 2025 20:38:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fish Schedule Async Tasks For End Of Tick

This is a half-solution for the plugins that try to read a world or block async.
This forces the async thread to wait until the world is done ticking (and is now safe to access), but also forces the "request" to be run in the world thread.
If I were to re-design this (which I will), I'll make it so async accesses are allowed while the level is not ticking (and therefore should be equivalent to Paper's).
Still, if an async access is done while the world is ticking, it will still have to schedule the "request" and wait.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
index 9d5c20282f88ed30db16cd6757e1bd3877957612..f369185156820a902fb3530c2ae6165bec77a695 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ServerLevel.java
@@ -842,7 +842,14 @@ public class ServerLevel extends Level implements ServerEntityGetter, WorldGenLe
         profilerFiller.push("entityManagement");
         // Paper - rewrite chunk system
         profilerFiller.pop();
+        // Fish start - Schedule tasks for end of tick
+        Runnable task;
+        while ((task = this._fish_endOfTickTasks.poll()) != null) {
+            task.run();
+        }
+        // Fish end - Schedule tasks for end of tick
     }
+    public final java.util.Queue<Runnable> _fish_endOfTickTasks = new java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>(); // Fish - Schedule tasks for end of tick
 
     @Override
     public boolean shouldTickBlocksAt(long chunkPos) {
